{"name":"Antelope","hex":"#b19664","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Antelope","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A census-designated place in Sacramento County, California, United States."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Antelope"}],"entries":[{"title":"Antelope","blocks":[{"text":"An antelope is any of the extant or recently extinct species of the ruminant artiodactyl family Bovidae, which are indigenous to most of Africa, India, the Middle East, Central Asia, and a small area of Russia. Antelopes do not form a monophyletic group, as some antelopes are more closely related to other bovid groups, such as bovines, goats, and sheep, than to other antelopes."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5e/Blackbuck_male_female.jpg/330px-Blackbuck_male_female.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Antelope","wikidata":"Q25894"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bb/Sable_bull.jpg/500px-Sable_bull.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bb/Sable_bull.jpg/1280px-Sable_bull.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bb/Sable_bull.jpg/500px-Sable_bull.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A bull sable antelope among the trees in the African savanna","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASable_bull.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f3/Topsell-5.jpg/500px-Topsell-5.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f3/Topsell-5.jpg/500px-Topsell-5.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Il